{
  "key": "letter-259-part-01",
  "number": 259,
  "generationId": "01a1e8fc-7c26-776b-9c3b-36aa817d1c3b",
  "voice": "Views",
  "speed": 0.9,
  "clips": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Love.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/01.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 0.619002
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Life becomes more authentic in the direct encountering of death.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/02.mp3",
      "start": 2.1704309999999998,
      "end": 5.993401
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "But we always try to escape the fact of death, and so life becomes pseudo and phony.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/03.mp3",
      "start": 7.381587,
      "end": 12.607211
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Even death, when authentic, has a beauty of its own while pseudo-life is just ugly.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/04.mp3",
      "start": 14.045986000000001,
      "end": 19.51059
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "Meditate on death because there is no way to know life unless you stand face to face with death.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/05.mp3",
      "start": 20.992313,
      "end": 26.347143000000003
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "And it is everywhere; wherever life is death is also.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/06.mp3",
      "start": 27.579501,
      "end": 32.114717
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "They are really two aspects of one and the same phenomenon,",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/07.mp3",
      "start": 33.420975000000006,
      "end": 36.739591999999995
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "and when one comes to know this, one transcends both.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/08.mp3",
      "start": 38.03381,
      "end": 42.318934
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "Only in that transcendence is the total flowering of consciousness and the ecstasy of being.",
      "path": "audio/1971-259/09.mp3",
      "start": 43.866599,
      "end": 50.42
    }
  ]
}
